WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:07.779
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and for my first
bonus video I thought it would be fun to rank

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:09.520
all 8 of the episodes from the first half
of the season.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.230
There were some inconsistencies with the pacing
but I’ll explain why everything landed where

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.230
it did.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:24.040
Since we’ve got 8 more weeks to go I’m
taking requests for bonus videos so drop all

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.690
your info bombs down in the comments.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:32.731
Just overall I though the first half of season
5 was better than most of season 4, the first

00:00:32.731 --> 00:00:33.731
and the second half.

00:00:33.731 --> 00:00:35.770
Most of that is due to what was going on with
the characters.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:40.590
I totally don’t mind them not doing explosions
as long as there are really strong character

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:51.910
moments I can fall in love with.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.760
Just a general spoiler warning for everything
through episode 8 on the show.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.870
Starting with Number 8 - Slabtown, Episode
4.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.020
Also known as the “Beth Episode”

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:03.770
Even Game of Thrones can’t top itself every
single week in terms of people’s body parts

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:08.600
getting eaten in front of them, so this at
the bottom just because the tone was so inconsistent

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.350
with the first three episodes and everything
after it.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:16.310
It’s like an island in a sea of crazy action,
but unlike the Governor last year.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:22.490
Beth or Emily Kinney just doesn’t have the
ability to hold screen time like David Morrissey.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.920
The reason why the Governor Episode was so
fascinating last year was because we were

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.420
seeing the evil king in exile.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.310
Regardless of what you thought of his character
arc, he was one of the more interesting characters.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:37.330
I think if Beth’s episode had been Carol’s
episode instead, if it had focused on Carol

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.170
exclusively and just explained Beth with a
few scenes.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.590
It would have ranked way way higher on my
list.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:46.140
Carol and Michonne are typically the people
you think about first when you think of interesting

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.550
female characters.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:51.560
And yes, I get why they wanted to do a “Beth
Episode”, but I feel like they could have

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.299
accomplished their goal of explaining her
story without having to lean so hard on such

00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:56.400
a weak character.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.369
And when I say Beth was weak, I just mean
underdeveloped.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:03.220
She lacked some of the complexities of Carol
and Michonne.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.259
There was almost no Pathos visible in Emily
Kinney’s performance.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:10.030
If she’d had another season, maybe she’d
have gotten there.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:17.120
All the other women on the show are going
through crucibles and coming out stronger.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.650
Beth just didn’t survive the trial by Hospital.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:25.450
And the only reason I think they killed her
was because they needed that place to feel

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.950
like a turning point for all the characters
and they didn’t want to make Rick too unlikable

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:36.689
by making him murder all those police officers
like he was the new governor or something.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:41.059
Although I don’t think The Governor or Shane
for that matter would have gone to the hospital

00:02:41.059 --> 00:02:52.170
to rescue Beth in the first place.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.659
Number 7 - Strangers, Episode 2 also known
as the “Gabriel Episode”

00:02:56.659 --> 00:03:00.489
I totally love Seth Gilliam as an actor, he
was awesome on The Wire, he was even good

00:03:00.489 --> 00:03:03.489
on Teen Wolf.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:08.370
But this episode was built around his character
and he is just pure walker bait at this point.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.849
Almost to the point where you root for him
to get eaten.

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:16.379
I loved the episode for being so faithful
to the comics, but this was a pretty weak

00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:19.069
follow up to the fiery escape from terminus.

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:34.900
And just to explain the logic here.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.549
None of these episodes were terrible, I even
liked the Beth episode.

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:40.769
But some of them were vastly better than the
others.

00:03:40.769 --> 00:03:45.599
And this one ended up being comic book fanservice
and a prologue for the Beth episodes and the

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:46.599
Hunters.

00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:57.889
Number 6 - The Mid Season Finale, Episode
8

00:03:57.889 --> 00:04:01.060
Why is this so low on my list?

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.499
Mostly because it was the most non-finale
ever.

00:04:04.499 --> 00:04:07.540
It was like the opposite of the premiere.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:13.200
That first episode ended in this fiery bloodbath
scattering the characters and decimating the

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.559
Terminus group.

00:04:14.559 --> 00:04:19.260
Metaphorically it was like watching a Lion
Roar out loud for 44 minutes until Morgan

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.691
came out and cracked his whip at it.

00:04:21.691 --> 00:04:23.560
They just set the bar too high for themselves.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:26.970
You just can’t follow that act with anything
that’s going to feel even bigger.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:34.210
Plus the budgets for premiere’s are usually
way higher just because they want to pull

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.380
in as many new viewers as possible.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:41.310
Blowing up all those evil termites was a huge
win for the characters.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:46.250
The ending of episode 8 was definitely not
a big win, for anyone.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.730
The survivors or the hospital people.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.600
Rewind to Season 4 and the prison battle.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.560
They gave the governor his big win.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.790
He got to destroy something Rick and the survivors
loved and rub it in their faces before he

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:58.790
died.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.810
I don’t count dying as a loss for him.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.900
The Governor definitely wanted to die in a
really passive kind of way.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:13.460
So I think he was kind of glad when Tara’s
sister finished him off.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:18.580
This year would have been different if Dawn
had been a stronger villain.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.830
But they were trying to be more ambiguous
about her alignment and instead, she ended

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:22.830
up feeling ineffectual.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.830
There are a number of reasons the writers
could have done that.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:27.260
But Robert Kirkman said we’re going to see
a new villain that will rival the Governor

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.250
in terms of ferocity.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:32.490
I just think they didn’t want Dawn to be
mistaken for that person.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:35.640
And they wanted Rick to seem like more of
a Shane.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:40.410
just to blur the lines between who was in
the right.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:43.560
Number 5 - Crossed, Episode 7, The Lead Up
to the Finale

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.840
It’s always harder to land the dismount
than it is to throw everyone into the air.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:53.330
So of course the anticipation was better.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.260
Plus all the melty walkers were just some
bad ass set design.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:00.470
I don’t always spend a lot of time talking
about the set design but in this case, the

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.800
walkers were above and beyond.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:08.100
Right up there with the waterlogged walkers
in Episode 2.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.610
Number 4 - Consumed, Episode 6

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:12.640
This was the Daryl and Carol episode.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.380
Little bit of fan service going on here, pairing
these two up in such an intimate way.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.190
But I thought it was a lot of fun and the
energy was great.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:25.240
We get Carol backstory like I wanted, some
funny Daryl jokes.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:29.410
Almost too subtle to be heard with human ears
and a lot of sentimentality.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:33.030
There are a couple of emotions I think go
really well with horror drama like Walking

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.030
Dead.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.590
Sadness and Sentimentality.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:37.200
Which are almost the same thing.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:43.960
I feel like they’re places to take the characters
that won’t step on the world they’ve created.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.360
Unlike the Beth Episode there was also some
real character development.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:50.700
We see Daryl and Carol both being victims
of abuse, learn from their past and grow.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:54.460
The most obvious sign, being Daryl snagging
the Book.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:58.190
Character development will always be my favorite
thing when there isn’t some major action

00:06:58.190 --> 00:06:59.190
set piece like the van going off the overpass.

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.420
Even if they didn’t put that in the episode
I would still have ranked this really high

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:14.660
on my list.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.660
Number 3 - Self Help, Episode 5

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:20.920
This was All Abraham’s Group and a whole
lot of crazy Abraham backstory.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:25.920
True to form, he’s pretty close to his character
in the comics.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.510
They kind of brushed over some of the details
in the flashbacks but they showed enough for

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.120
us to get the message.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.389
Abraham is every bit as delusional as Eugene.

00:07:34.389 --> 00:07:38.550
Michael Cudlitz also got way more active on
social media this year so it’s fun to watch

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:42.639
him react to Abraham months after he’s filmed
his scenes.

00:07:42.639 --> 00:07:45.860
One of the other big reasons this made it
so high on my list was the Eugene Reveal.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:49.610
The minute he showed up all the comic book
readers knew the drill.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:53.650
But I all but forgot about it after the end
of season 4.

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:57.350
Josh McDermitt just hypnotizes you with that
mullet speak.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:59.400
Which actually makes some sense.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.030
It does flow from factual information.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:05.960
He just delivers it in a way that makes it
a billion times more confusing than it needs

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:06.960
to be.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.450
That’s his magic.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.850
He really grew on me in this episode.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:13.460
Especially his relationship with Tara.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:16.320
They’re my new favorite non-sexual couple.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:19.540
The actors kind of described it as a brother
sister thing.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:23.520
The Pervert moment was probably one of my
favorite funny moments from any of the season

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.520
5 episodes.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:29.370
And no, Tara catching him is in no way going
to deter him from trying to peep on abraham

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:30.370
and rosita.

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:35.449
Although he’s probably going to keep himself
out of punching distance for the next couple

00:08:35.449 --> 00:08:36.800
of episodes.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.809
Number 2 - Four Walls and A Roof, Episode
3

00:08:39.809 --> 00:08:42.009
You could also call this Fear the Hunters.

00:08:42.009 --> 00:08:47.139
This would have been a great midseason finale
episode.

00:08:47.139 --> 00:08:51.040
Rick and the survivors taking the Hunters
Down, Rick’s machete moment with Gareth.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:52.350
Tainted Meat.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:56.060
Such an apropos adaptation of a comic book
storyline.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:59.420
Maybe the fact that they didn’t make us
wait for the payoff and killing bob is what

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:02.399
boosted this up my list.

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:12.180
But I think they ran into problems by putting
the beth episode right after it when the abraham

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:17.839
episode would have been a smoother transition
from epic WTF to less life threatening screams

00:09:17.839 --> 00:09:19.800
of horror.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.990
Finding out Eugene was lying was a horrific
moment for abraham, but at least someone wasn’t

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:25.641
eating his messed up hand in front of him.

00:09:25.641 --> 00:09:29.019
Of all the episode to re-watch while we’re
waiting for the season to come back.

00:09:29.019 --> 00:09:30.740
This would probably be at the top of my list.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:34.339
The only reason this wasn’t my number one
episode is because the escape from terminus

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:38.040
was like a 44 minute long scream of joy and
terror.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.140
You get so cranked up you can’t tell if
you’re really freaked out or really happy.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:46.100
Which is why my Number 1 episode so far was
the premiere.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:50.460
I’d say this is as close to a perfect beginning
to a new season as you could do.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:53.600
The downside being, that you make it almost
impossible to one-up yourself.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:57.519
And you run the chance that everything after
feels like a letdown.

00:09:57.519 --> 00:10:02.610
Thankfully we got Fear the Hunters, Team Daryl
and Carol and Eugene versus Abraham.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:05.149
They spent all this time teasing Terminus
last year.

00:10:05.149 --> 00:10:07.069
8 episodes building to something.

00:10:07.069 --> 00:10:08.069
Then kaboom.

00:10:08.069 --> 00:10:09.980
They just blew it up right after they got
there.

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:13.450
Of all the ways we’ve been jerked around
by the show, this was the best.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:15.889
Just as a point of reference, the opposite
of that.

00:10:15.889 --> 00:10:20.230
The worst moment of us being jerked around
was going from Fear the Hunters to a Downer

00:10:20.230 --> 00:11:45.019
Beth episode.

